This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   - Continued from previous session: run linter and commit the `feature/card-row-layout` branch, then create a PR (#25)
   - Fix board/other pages looking "ugly" compared to the Dashboard (glassmorphism per-card → flat rows)
   - Sort milestone groups descending by version number, `(No Milestone)` pinned first
   - Create new branch `feature/perf-loading` to improve slow project loading
   - Implement progressive loading: show board after first GraphQL page, defer linked PRs to background
   - Add stale-while-revalidate cache with `globalState` + `dataComplete` loading indicator
   - Create PR #26 for perf branch
   - Fix all 6 Copilot review comments on PR #26

   **IMPORTANT SECURITY/PREFERENCE NOTE (verbatim):** Never add `Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>` to any commit message.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - VSCode Webview Extension (React + TypeScript)
   - CSS Grid layout with `lp-*` classes shared between `LaunchpadView` (dashboard) and `ItemCard` (board)
   - Glassmorphism: `backdrop-filter`, gradient borders, `::before`/`::after` pseudo-elements
   - Stale-while-revalidate cache pattern using `vscode.ExtensionContext.globalState`
   - Progressive/streaming data delivery via `onPage` callback on GraphQL pagination
   - Incremental state accumulation to avoid O(n²) rebuilding on each page
   - `dataComplete` message signal for background-fetch completion
   - Sprint auto-select deferral to ensure full dataset is known before committing
   - GitHub GraphQL Projects V2 API pagination (100 items/page)
   - Promise.all vs sequential async patterns for background enrichment
   - Scoped cache keys to avoid cross-project data contamination

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **`webview-ui/components/ItemCard.tsx`** (feature/card-row-layout, already committed)
     - Fully rewritten to use `lp-*` CSS grid classes matching `LaunchpadView`
     - 7-column grid: age | status icons | title+labels | diff | author | assignees | repo/branch
     - Added `timeAgo`, `CIDot`, `ReviewDot` helpers

   - **`webview-ui/styles.css`** (feature/card-row-layout, then perf branch)
     - `.col-group`: changed to `border: 1px solid #2a2a3d; border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden; margin-bottom: 8px`
     - `.col-header`: `padding: 7px 12px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.015); border-bottom: 1px solid #1e1e2e`
     - `.col-items`: `padding: 0`
     - `.item-card`: flat row with `border-bottom: 1px solid #1a1a2e` only (no background, no border-radius)
     - `.item-card:hover`: `background: rgba(137,180,250,0.06)`
     - All `.liquid-glass .item-card` heavy glass effects removed; replaced with simple flat rules
     - Added `.footer-loading-more`, `.footer-loading-dot`, `@keyframes footerPulse`:
     ```css
     .footer-loading-dot {
       width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 50%;
       background: #89b4fa;
       animation: footerPulse 1.2s ease-in-out infinite;
     }
     @keyframes footerPulse {
       0%, 100% { opacity: 0.3; transform: scale(0.85); }
       50%       { opacity: 1;   transform: scale(1); }
     }
     ```

   - **`webview-ui/App.tsx`**
     - Milestone sort added before `Object.entries(milestoneGroups).map(...)`:
     ```typescript
     .sort(([a], [b]) => {
       if (a === '(No Milestone)') return -1;
       if (b === '(No Milestone)') return 1;
       const parts = (s: string) => s.split('.').map((n) => parseInt(n, 10) || 0);
       const ap = parts(a), bp = parts(b);
       for (let i = 0; i < Math.max(ap.length, bp.length); i++) {
         const diff = (bp[i] ?? 0) - (ap[i] ?? 0);
         if (diff !== 0) return diff;
       }
       return 0;
     })
     ```
     - Added `isLoadingMore` state and `dataRef = React.useRef<RunwayData | null>(null)`
     - Message handlers updated:
       - `case 'loading'`: `setIsLoadingMore(true)` (removed `setIsRefreshing`)
       - `case 'refreshing'`: `setIsLoadingMore(true)`
       - `case 'dataComplete'`: `setIsLoadingMore(false); setIsRefreshing(false)` + sprint auto-select
       - `case 'data'`: `dataRef.current = msg.payload`; only validates existing sprint selection (no auto-select)
       - `case 'linkedIssuePRs'`: `setData((prev) => prev ? { ...prev, linkedIssuePRs: msg.prs } : null)`
     - Sprint auto-select deferred to `dataComplete`:
     ```typescript
     case 'dataComplete':
       setIsLoadingMore(false);
       setIsRefreshing(false);
       if (sprintNeedsAutoSelect.current && dataRef.current?.sprints.length) {
         sprintNeedsAutoSelect.current = false;
         const { sprints } = dataRef.current;
         setSprintFilter((prev) => {
           if (prev !== null) return sprints.includes(prev) ? prev : (sprints[0] ?? null);
           return sprints[0] ?? null;
         });
       }
       break;
     ```
     - Footer loading indicator:
     ```tsx
     {isLoadingMore && (
       <span className="footer-loading-more" title="Fetching latest data…">
         <span className="footer-loading-dot" />
         Updating…
       </span>
     )}
     ```

   - **`src/githubService.ts`** (feature/perf-loading)
     - `buildRunwayData(nodes, statusFieldName, ...)` replaced with `assembleRunwayData(groups, sprintsSet, projectTitle, viewerLogin, rateLimit)` — only does ordering/sorting, no node parsing
     - `fetchProjectData` now accumulates groups/sprints incrementally:
     ```typescript
     const groups: Record<string, BoardItem[]> = {};
     const sprintsSet = new Set<string>();
     do {
       // fetch page...
       for (const node of project.items.nodes) {
         const column = extractColumn(node, statusFieldName);
         const item = parseItem(node, column);
         if (!item) continue;
         if (!groups[column]) groups[column] = [];
         groups[column].push(item);
         if (item.sprint) sprintsSet.add(item.sprint);
       }
       cursor = project.items.pageInfo.hasNextPage ? project.items.pageInfo.endCursor : null;
       onPage?.(assembleRunwayData(groups, sprintsSet, projectTitle, viewerLogin, lastRateLimit));
     } while (cursor !== null);
     return assembleRunwayData(groups, sprintsSet, projectTitle, viewerLogin, lastRateLimit);
     ```
     - Added `fetchLinkedPRsForBoard(groups)` exported function
     - CodeOwners parallelized: `const [a, b, c] = await Promise.all([tryPath('.github/CODEOWNERS'), tryPath('CODEOWNERS'), tryPath('docs/CODEOWNERS')]); const content = a ?? b ?? c;`

   - **`src/types.ts`** (feature/perf-loading)
     - Added to `ExtensionMessage`:
     ```typescript
     | { type: 'refreshing' }
     | { type: 'dataComplete' }
     | { type: 'linkedIssuePRs'; prs: BoardItem[] }
     ```

   - **`src/SprintHubPanel.ts`** (feature/perf-loading)
     - Added `private readonly _context: vscode.ExtensionContext`
     - `createOrShow` and constructor now accept `context: vscode.ExtensionContext`
     - `CACHE_KEY` replaced with scoped method:
     ```typescript
     private static _cacheKey(owner: string, projectNumber: number, ownerType: string, statusFieldName: string): string {
       return `sprinthub.cache.${owner}.${projectNumber}.${ownerType}.${statusFieldName}`;
     }
     ```
     - `_loadData` now:
       1. Computes `cacheKey` from config
       2. Loads cached data → posts `data` + calls `_updateStatusBar(cached)` + posts `refreshing`
       3. Falls back to posting `loading` if no cache
       4. Fetches progressively with `onPage` callback
       5. Saves to cache with `.then(undefined, err => console.error(...))` rejection handling
       6. Runs background enrichment sequentially:
     ```typescript
     void (async () => {
       try {
         const linkedPRs = await this._fetchLinkedPRsBackground(data.groups);
         await this._checkConflicts({ ...data, linkedIssuePRs: linkedPRs });
       } finally {
         this._post({ type: 'dataComplete' });
       }
     })();
     ```
     - `_fetchLinkedPRsBackground` now returns `Promise<BoardItem[]>` instead of `Promise<void>`

   - **`src/extension.ts`** (feature/perf-loading)
     - `SprintHubPanel.createOrShow(context.extensionUri, context)` (added context)

4. Errors and Fixes:
   - **`isLoadingMore` declared but never read** (TypeScript hint): Fixed by wiring it into message handlers (`setIsLoadingMore(true/false)`) and using it in the footer JSX
   - **`dataRef` declared but never read** (TypeScript hint): Fixed by setting `dataRef.current = msg.payload` in the `data` handler and reading it in `dataComplete` for auto-select
   - **Copilot review comment: cache key not scoped**: Fixed by replacing static `CACHE_KEY` with `_cacheKey(owner, projectNumber, ownerType, statusFieldName)` method
   - **Copilot review comment: conflicts miss linked PRs**: Fixed by running `_checkConflicts` after `_fetchLinkedPRsBackground` resolves, passing `{ ...data, linkedIssuePRs: linkedPRs }`
   - **Copilot review comment: `void globalState.update()`**: Fixed with `.then(undefined, err => console.error(...))`
   - **Copilot review comment: O(n²) rebuild**: Fixed by incremental accumulation — only new nodes parsed per page
   - **Copilot review comment: wrong sprint auto-selected**: Fixed by deferring auto-select to `dataComplete`
   - **Copilot review comment: status bar not updated from cache**: Fixed by adding `this._updateStatusBar(cached)` after posting cached data

5. Problem Solving:
   - **Board cards "ugly"**: Root cause was per-card glassmorphism creating "glass inside glass". Solved by making `col-group` the glass container and `item-card` flat transparent rows, matching the dashboard's `lp-group`/`lp-row` pattern
   - **Slow project loading**: Root cause was waiting for all GraphQL pages + linked PR fetch before posting anything. Solved by (1) progressive page delivery via `onPage` callback, (2) stale-while-revalidate cache showing last board instantly, (3) background enrichment with `dataComplete` signal
   - **O(n²) page building**: Solved by accumulating groups/sprints incrementally instead of re-parsing all nodes on every page
   - **Sprint auto-select on partial first page**: Solved by deferring auto-select to `dataComplete` using a `dataRef` to access latest data without stale closures

6. All User Messages:
   - (Session restoration — automated context summary provided)
   - Screenshot of Dashboard + board with caption: "Dashboard looks nice. But every other pages looks ugly"
   - "On the milestone page, can we order from latest (highest)? And keep the `No Milestone` first"
   - "Create a PR"
   - "Is there a way to improve the loading of a whole project, I mean it's super slow ..."
   - "Let's implement it then in a new branch"
   - "ok it is still slow. Can we: Load 1 page of GraphQL, then show webview, and make it lazyload kinda"
   - "ok create a pr for it"
   - (User opened `package.json` in IDE) + shared PR review URL: "Can you check this review for the current pr"
   - "Yes of course" (in response to "Want me to address all 6 review comments?")
   - (Summary request)

7. Pending Tasks:
   - **Push `feature/perf-loading` after review fixes**: The commit `e5f84b1` was made but `git push` was not called after it. The branch needs to be pushed to update PR #26 with all 6 fixes.

8. Current Work:
   The immediately prior work was implementing all 6 Copilot review fixes for PR #26 (`feature/perf-loading`). All fixes were implemented and committed in `e5f84b1` "fix: address all 6 Copilot review comments":

   - **Fix 1** (scoped cache key): `src/SprintHubPanel.ts` — replaced `CACHE_KEY` static with `_cacheKey(owner, projectNumber, ownerType, statusFieldName)` method
   - **Fix 2** (conflicts after linked PRs): Sequential IIFE — `const linkedPRs = await _fetchLinkedPRsBackground(...)` then `await _checkConflicts({ ...data, linkedIssuePRs: linkedPRs })`
   - **Fix 3** (void update rejection): `.then(undefined, err => console.error(...))`
   - **Fix 4** (incremental O(n)): `assembleRunwayData(groups, sprintsSet, ...)` + per-page node parsing in `src/githubService.ts`
   - **Fix 5** (sprint auto-select deferred): `dataRef.current` set in `data` handler, auto-select runs in `dataComplete` handler in `webview-ui/App.tsx`
   - **Fix 6** (status bar from cache): `this._updateStatusBar(cached)` added in `src/SprintHubPanel.ts`

   TypeScript and lint both passed clean (`npx tsc --noEmit` no errors, `npm run lint` only pre-existing warnings in `SettingsPanel.tsx`).

9. Optional Next Step:
   Push the review fix commit to update PR #26:
   ```
   git push
   ```
   This directly follows from: "Yes of course" (fix all 6 review comments) — all fixes are committed locally but the branch has not been pushed since `e5f84b1`.

