{"body":"## Pull request overview

This PR improves the SprintHub extension’s perceived performance by showing cached/partial board data quickly, progressively streaming paginated results to the webview, and fetching linked PR enrichment in the background with UI loading indicators.

**Changes:**
- Adds progressive board delivery (`fetchProjectData` now emits partial pages) and a background linked-PR enrichment step.
- Implements board caching via VS Code `globalState` and updates the webview messaging protocol (`refreshing`, `dataComplete`, `linkedIssuePRs`).
- Updates the webview UI to reflect background loading state in the footer.

### Reviewed changes

Copilot reviewed 6 out of 9 changed files in this pull request and generated 6 comments.

<details>
<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>

| File | Description |
| ---- | ----------- |
| webview-ui/styles.css | Adds footer loading indicator styles and animation. |
| webview-ui/App.tsx | Adds new message handling + footer “Updating…” indicator for progressive/background loads. |
| src/types.ts | Extends extension→webview message union with progressive-load and enrichment message types. |
| src/SprintHubPanel.ts | Adds cached-first rendering, progressive posting of pages, and background linked-PR enrichment. |
| src/githubService.ts | Refactors board construction into `buildRunwayData`, adds `onPage` progressive callback, and adds `fetchLinkedPRsForBoard`. |
| src/extension.ts | Passes `ExtensionContext` into panel creation to enable caching. |
</details>







---

