This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   - Started by pushing `feature/perf-loading` to update PR #26 with 6 Copilot review fixes
   - Created `feature/glass-standup-modal` branch to improve the standup modal's glass appearance (chromatic dispersion, animated specular, blur localization)
   - Applied glass badge treatment to `.label`, `.badge-sprint`, `.badge-milestone`, `.lp-draft-badge` following Ein UI patterns
   - Added glass skeleton loading screen (replaced spinner) and skeleton-loading-more for refresh state
   - Fixed modal to be truly transparent: overlay blurs the board, modal is a thin glass pane (no backdrop-filter on modal itself)
   - Fixed skeleton appearing above content instead of below
   - Fixed `isLoadingMore` starting `false` (race condition) → changed to `useState(true)`
   - Fixed auto-refresh clearing the board: added `isRefreshingRef` to buffer page updates during refresh, apply atomically at `dataComplete`
   - Switched to `feature/perf-loading` to address 3 new PR #26 review comments: `_lastData` unused, sprint null override, `onPage` serialization overhead
   - Returned to `feature/glass-standup-modal`, fixed base (non-liquid-glass) standup modal to also be transparent
   - **Most recent**: User identified that auto-refresh progressive loading still causes issues — wants `onPage` callback only for initial load (no cache), not for refresh (has cache)

   **IMPORTANT SECURITY/PREFERENCE NOTE (verbatim):** Never add `Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>` to any commit message.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - VSCode Webview Extension (React + TypeScript)
   - Glassmorphism: `backdrop-filter`, gradient borders, `::before`/`::after` pseudo-elements
   - Key glass insight: overlay blurs the board, modal itself has `backdrop-filter: none` + near-zero background alpha — the overlay's blur is what creates the frosted effect; modal's own blur would just blur the overlay dim color
   - Chromatic dispersion: directional `inset` box-shadows (blue top-left, violet bottom-right), `::after` radial gradients
   - Animated specular: `@keyframes glassSheen { 0%, 100% { opacity: 0.75; } 50% { opacity: 1; } }` on `::before`
   - Shimmer animation: `@keyframes shimmer { 0% { background-position: 200% 0; } 100% { background-position: -200% 0; } }`
   - Stale-while-revalidate cache: `vscode.ExtensionContext.globalState`
   - Progressive loading: `onPage` callback on GraphQL pagination
   - `isRefreshingRef` pattern: buffer `setData()` calls during refresh, apply atomically at `dataComplete`
   - `isLoadingMore = useState(true)` so skeleton is always visible from first `data` message
   - `sprintNeedsAutoSelect` ref: prevents auto-select overriding explicit user "All sprints" choice
   - `onPage` throttle: page 1 always delivered, then every 3rd page (`pageCount % 3 === 0 || cursor === null`)

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **`webview-ui/styles.css`** (feature/glass-standup-modal)
     - Base standup modal (transparent, no backdrop-filter):
     ```css
     .standup-overlay {
       background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.28);
       backdrop-filter: blur(10px) saturate(160%) brightness(0.82);
       -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(10px) saturate(160%) brightness(0.82);
       z-index: 400; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding: 20px;
     }
     .standup-modal {
       background: rgba(16, 18, 44, 0.18);
       backdrop-filter: none;
       border: 1.5px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.12);
       border-radius: 14px;
       width: 580px; max-width: 100%; max-height: 80vh; display: flex; flex-direction: column;
       animation: fadeScaleIn 0.18s ease;
       box-shadow: 0 32px 80px rgba(0,0,0,0.40), inset 0 1.5px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.14);
     }
     ```
     - Liquid-glass standup modal:
     ```css
     .liquid-glass .standup-overlay {
       backdrop-filter: blur(10px) saturate(150%) brightness(0.80) !important;
       background: rgba(0,0,0,0.22) !important;
     }
     .liquid-glass .standup-modal {
       backdrop-filter: none !important;
       background: rgba(16,16,36,0.18) padding-box,
         linear-gradient(148deg, rgba(255,255,255,0.55) 0%, rgba(255,255,255,0.10) 40%, rgba(0,0,0,0.28) 100%) border-box !important;
       box-shadow: 0 32px 80px rgba(0,0,0,0.35), inset 0 2px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.22),
         inset 6px 6px 40px rgba(100,160,255,0.04), inset -6px -6px 40px rgba(203,166,247,0.04) !important;
     }
     .liquid-glass .standup-modal::before { /* animated specular sheen */
       animation: glassSheen 5s ease-in-out infinite;
       background: linear-gradient(155deg, rgba(255,255,255,0.18) 0%, rgba(255,255,255,0.05) 40%, transparent 100%);
     }
     .liquid-glass .standup-modal::after { /* chromatic dispersion */
       background: radial-gradient(ellipse 55% 40% at 0% 0%, rgba(100,160,255,0.07) 0%, transparent 100%),
         radial-gradient(ellipse 50% 40% at 100% 100%, rgba(203,166,247,0.07) 0%, transparent 100%),
         radial-gradient(ellipse 70% 50% at 50% 110%, rgba(137,180,250,0.08) 0%, transparent 100%);
     }
     ```
     - Glass badges: `.liquid-glass .badge-sprint` uses `backdrop-filter: blur(20px) saturate(200%)`, `background: rgba(137,180,250,0.12)`, `box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.14), 0 2px 8px rgba(137,180,250,0.12)`
     - Glass skeleton: `.skeleton-pulse::before` uses shimmer animation, liquid-glass version uses blue-tinted shimmer `rgba(137,180,250,0.12)`
     - Skeleton-loading-more: `.skeleton-loading-more { padding: 6px 16px 14px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; }`

   - **`webview-ui/App.tsx`** (feature/glass-standup-modal)
     - `isLoadingMore` initialized to `true`: `const [isLoadingMore, setIsLoadingMore] = useState(true);`
     - `isRefreshingRef` added: `const isRefreshingRef = useRef(false);`
     - Message handler with refresh buffering:
     ```typescript
     case 'loading':
       isRefreshingRef.current = false;
       setIsLoadingMore(true);
       if (state !== 'data') setState('loading');
       break;
     case 'refreshing':
       isRefreshingRef.current = true;
       setIsLoadingMore(true);
       break;
     case 'dataComplete': {
       isRefreshingRef.current = false;
       setIsLoadingMore(false);
       setIsRefreshing(false);
       const final = dataRef.current;
       if (final) {
         setData(final);
         setState('data');
         setDetailItem((prev) => { /* sync with fresh data */ });
       }
       if (final?.sprints.length) {
         const { sprints } = final;
         setSprintFilter((prev) => {
           if (sprintNeedsAutoSelect.current) {
             sprintNeedsAutoSelect.current = false;
             return prev !== null && sprints.includes(prev) ? prev : (sprints[0] ?? null);
           }
           if (prev === null) return null;
           return sprints.includes(prev) ? prev : (sprints[0] ?? null);
         });
       }
       break;
     }
     case 'data': {
       dataRef.current = msg.payload;
       if (isRefreshingRef.current) break; // buffer during refresh
       setData(msg.payload);
       setState('data');
       // setSprintFilter and setDetailItem sync...
       break;
     }
     ```
     - Initial skeleton board (state === 'loading'):
     ```tsx
     {state === 'loading' && (
       <div className="skeleton-board">
         {[0, 1, 2].map((gi) => (
           <div key={gi} className="skeleton-group">
             <div className="skeleton-col-header" />
