     owner, projectNumber, ownerType === 'organization', statusFieldName,
     (partial) => {
       this._post({ type: 'data', payload: partial });
       this._updateStatusBar(partial);
     }
   );
   ```

   The fix needed: only use `onPage` when no cache exists (initial load). When refreshing (cache exists), pass `undefined` so `fetchProjectData` accumulates all pages internally and returns once — then post one `data` message.

9. Optional Next Step:
   Implement the auto-refresh bulk-fetch fix in `src/SprintHubPanel.ts`. The user said: "I would rather keep a huge call for the auto-refresh, otherwise there are few minutes where we see nothing in the listing."

